--- event pkid.crl.published
tier: standard
gating: none
cardinality: once per CRL

A CA signed a new CRL, on pkid's own schedule or at an officer's request,
and pkid handed it to its publishers.

include: subject.token.sid, object.pkid.ca, object.pkid.number, object.pkid.next_update

--- event pkid.crl.expiring
tier: standard
gating: none
cardinality: at most daily per CA

A CA's CRL is running out. For a CA whose key is in a sealed file, from 30
days before it expires: an officer has to sign a new one with `pki ca
publish-crl`. For a CA whose key pkid keeps, once three quarters of its
life has passed, which means pkid's own renewal has been failing. Also
emitted for a CA that has distribution points but no CRL.

include: subject.token.sid, object.pkid.ca, object.pkid.next_update

--- field subject.token.sid
type: str

The SID of the principal that made the request: the requester of a
submission, or the officer who decided, revoked or published. pkid's own
service SID for what pkid did on its own schedule.

pkid reads it from the token the kernel captured when the caller connected.

--- field object.pkid.ca
type: str

The identifier of the CA the request was made to, its key under
Machine\Software\Pki\Authorities.

--- field object.pkid.request
type: int

The CA database's number for the request. Numbers are assigned in order and
never reused.

--- field object.pkid.outcome
type: str.enum
values: issued | pending | denied
closed: true

What policy decided for a submitted request: issued at once, held for an
officer, or refused.

--- field object.pkid.serial
type: bin

The revoked certificate's serial number, as the big-endian integer encoded in
the certificate.

--- field object.pkid.reason
type: uint

The RFC 5280 revocation reason code.

--- field object.pkid.number
type: uint

The CRL's number. Each CA numbers its CRLs from 1, and a number is never
reused.

--- field object.pkid.next_update
type: int

When the CRL expires, in seconds since the Unix epoch. Absent when the CA
has no CRL.

--- field object.pkid.action
type: str.enum
values: created | imported | installed | configured | secured | signed-subordinate | exported-key
closed: true

What was done to the CA: created with a new key, imported from a sealed key
file, given the certificate it awaited, given new templates or distribution
points, given a new security descriptor, used to sign a subordinate CA
elsewhere, or its key exported.

--- field outcome.success
type: bool

Whether pkid can serve the configuration it loaded.

--- field outcome.reason
type: str

Why the configuration can't be served: the first record found invalid, by
its key below Machine\Software\Pki.

--- event pkid.configuration.loaded
tier: standard
gating: none
cardinality: once at start and once per configuration change

pkid read its configuration from the Registry.

A configuration that can't be served stops pkid issuing until it is
corrected; pkid never issues from part of one. Who changed the configuration
is recorded by the Registry's own audit, not here.

include: outcome.success, outcome.reason

--- event pkid.request.submitted
tier: standard
gating: none
cardinality: once per recorded request

A request was submitted and recorded with its outcome.

Requests refused before they are recorded, for lack of the Request right or
for naming a template the CA doesn't offer, appear only in the kernel's
access audit.

include: subject.token.sid, object.pkid.ca, object.pkid.request, object.pkid.outcome

--- event pkid.request.approved
tier: standard
gating: none
cardinality: once per approval

An officer approved a held request, and its certificate was issued.

include: subject.token.sid, object.pkid.ca, object.pkid.request

--- event pkid.request.denied
tier: standard
gating: none
cardinality: once per denial

An officer denied a held request.

include: subject.token.sid, object.pkid.ca, object.pkid.request

--- event pkid.authority.changed
tier: standard
gating: none
cardinality: once per management operation

An administrator created, imported, installed or reconfigured a CA, changed
who may use it, had it sign a subordinate CA elsewhere, or exported its key.

include: subject.token.sid, object.pkid.ca, object.pkid.action

--- event pkid.certificate.revoked
tier: standard
gating: none
cardinality: once per revocation

An officer revoked a certificate.

include: subject.token.sid, object.pkid.ca, object.pkid.serial, object.pkid.reason
